so last night was the second night of  the democratic national convention we  had a live stream for the full two hours  there was the sort of formal  nomination process of joe biden with  each state casting their delegates  uh proportionally or 100 for different  candidates and  it was a significantly better night than  night one without question  there were fewer of these energy sucking  moments where after like an okay speech  they would cut to  low energy smooth jazz or something like  that  it was better put together there were  actually some very interesting moments  headlined by  joe biden's wife dr jill biden who did  the last speech of the night who i  realized  in watching her she would be a better  president  than donald trump forget about joe biden  for a moment  i was trying to think is there any issue  where if you said  david we need either donald trump or  jill  biden to figure out this issue is there  any issue where i would pick donald  trump and there really isn't  i mean even on coronavirus quite frankly  it's hard to imagine anyone doing a  worse job than  trump on the virus but as a doctor of  education  jill biden would just understand oh it's  a medical situation oh well we need to  let doctors take the lead rather than  than donald trump for example but i'm  heading  getting ahead of myself a little bit  here one of the best moments  was one of the best lines of the night  really was former secretary  of state john kerry referring to donald  trump's overseas trips as blooper reels  take a look at this  donald trump inherited a growing economy  and a more peaceful world  and like everything else he inherited he  bankrupted it  when this president goes overseas it  isn't a goodwill mission it's a blooper  reel  he breaks up with our allies and writes  love letters to dictators  america deserves a president who is  looked up to  not laughed at that actually made me  laugh in in the moment and john kerry  uh was was quite good at laying out the  importance of voting  uh for joe biden and to remove donald  trump in november bill clinton also  spoke and it was fine  there was debate about whether bill  clinton should speak or maybe instead it  should be al gore  who is sort of a direct testament to  what happens when not enough people vote  and you end up winning the popular vote  losing the electoral college and  changing the course of history maybe al  gore should have spoken instead maybe al  gore  should have spoken in addition to bill  clinton we heard from congresswoman  alexandria ocasio-cortez in a much  anticipated speech it was very short  she formally nominated bernie sanders to  be the nominee there were some people  who said oh it's a snub  it was really a formality bernie was set  to receive delegates from some states so  someone has to nominate him  it was not a snub it was rather  procedural and  nbc news took some heat because they  misreported  what alexandria ocasio-cortez did and  they made a big deal out of it  i'm not going to since it really wasn't  a big deal and i don't want to play  into that but we did hear from aoc and  then yeah dr jill biden let's take a  look at just a little bit of her speech  and you'll see  this is the wrap up and you'll see joe  biden come out and embrace her if you're  watching and you'll hear him say just a  few words  if you are listening i know that if we  entrust this nation to joe  he will do for your family what he did  for ours bring us together  and make us whole carry us forward  in our time of need keep the promise  of america for all of us  hey everyone i'm jill biden's husband  as you heard tonight excuse me you can  see why she's the love of my life  the rock of our family she never gives  herself much credit  but the truth is she's the strongest  person i know she's a backbone like a  ramrod  she loves fiercely cares deeply nothing  stops her when she sets her mind into  getting something right  so yeah i mean it's all pretty cheesy  this this isn't the type of packaging  that appeals to me  this isn't the type of political event  that appeals to me  but it doesn't matter i'm not the target  here and realistically  neither are you realistically anybody  who is  watching the david pakman show on  youtube listens to political podcasts if  you listen to the podcast  you're not the target you you've already  decided right and so i think it's  important for us to keep that in mind  but i have to say  when you hear about and learn about  the tragedy of joe biden's life losing  his first wife and child  in a car accident and then you hear  about jill biden  becoming a mother to joe biden's two  sons while she was in graduate school  you just see the way the bidens relate  to each other it is a reminder because  of the stark contrast that's in the  white house right now  about how absurd the trump  administration and trump as president is  on a personal level melania seems to  hate trump  some of trump's kids seem to hate him  trump  seems to think some of his kids are  idiots like not none of this is normal  and obviously we can separate  you know if their politics are great who  cares about their home lives  in this particular case with donald  trump it's all related  and it's all very very bad the same  delusions of grandeur and narcissism  that make his f a personal life and  family life a disaster  make his administration a disaster and  that was  you know i i didn't really need the  convention because the choices are so  crystal clear for me this time around  but i do think that this second night  particularly with dr jill biden and some  of the backstory on joe biden's life  i do think it actually was far better  put together  than night number one so tonight we're  going to be hearing from  senator elizabeth warren which i'm very  much looking forward to again  as someone who competed against joe  biden in the democratic primary this  year  we heard from by uh bernie on monday  night  making the case that if you supported  bernie in 2016 if you supported bernie  in 2020  here is why it is so important to vote  for joe biden in november  i'm interested to see how elizabeth  warren  puts together a sort of similar argument  i'm not as much  looking forward to hearing from nancy  pelosi and hillary clinton tonight  although i think it will be interesting  to see what approach they take  and whether they play to the left or  they play to the middle or what they do  we're going to hear from former  congresswoman grab gabby giffords who  is a tragically was a victim of gun  violence years ago  and also headlining tonight we will hear  from vice presidential candidate  kamala harris and we're also going to  hear from former president barack obama  all leading up to the final night  tomorrow  when we will hear from the nominee  himself  joe biden and it's much anticipated  for different reasons by different  people the right is anticipating joe  biden's speech  with the idea that he's going to be  barely coherent and  unable to put together anything sensible  or sensical  whereas i'm interested in seeing what is  the  approach in order to bring people in  in other words centrists center left  disaffected republicans progressive  leftists former bernie people  so on and so forth so i will see you  tonight  at 8 45 pm eastern time on youtube  twitch  and or facebook your preference uh for  the start of night three  and um we will be back of course  tomorrow with analysis and preparation  for the final night of the democratic  national convention  and then we have to get ready for the  republican national convention happening  next week
 

